# The CRM's source. It is in the repository so it can be worked on, and it is
# bundled into crm/ by tools/build-crm.sh — which is what actually ships.
#
# Without this line Vercel would serve it too, and /crm-src/ would be a second
# working copy of the application on the same host: outside the /crm/ header
# rule, so without its Content-Security-Policy and without its noindex.
crm-src

# Plans, notes and the source-of-truth document are for whoever works on this,
# not for whoever visits it.
*.md
!README.md

# Skills, their reference material and their starter files. Tooling for
# whoever works on this repository, and several of the starters are HTML —
# without this they would be served from the website's own domain.
.claude

# Source material, not the site. The root JPEGs are the unprocessed originals
# (the page serves the webp derivatives in assets/img) and two of them —
# structure.jpeg and crane.jpeg — are stock-style collages that are NOT
# Kingson's work and must never be served from Kingson's domain. The zip is an
# archive of an earlier build. tools/ is the build and the publication gate;
# nothing in the browser imports it.
/*.jpeg
/*.jpg
/*.zip
tools
.gitattributes
